    ("What else often forms besides the gas?", "A salt?", "Acid + metal → salt + hydrogen. Family?", "Not a type of light?", "They form only water always, no salt.", "A salt.", "That's it — salt plus hydrogen."),
    ("How do we test hydrogen in school?", "A burning splint gives a pop?", "Pop test. Hydrogen?", "Not limewater?", "Hydrogen turns limewater milky.", "The pop with a lighted splint.", "That's it — pop test for hydrogen."),
    ("Does every metal behave the same?", "Less reactive metals may barely react?", "Copper vs magnesium. Different?", "Reactivity series later?", "All metals explode identically in acid.", "No — reactivity differs.", "That's it — metals differ."),
    ("Is this the same as acid + base?", "No — metal reaction makes hydrogen; neutralization makes water (and salt)?", "Two families. Unmix?", "Stay on chemistry.", "They are identical reactions.", "No — different reaction families.", "That's it — you unmixed metal vs base."),
    ("What does 'reactive metal' mean here?", "A metal that more readily displaces hydrogen from the acid?", "Mg vs Cu. Who fizzes?", "Not a personality?", "Reactive means the metal is wet.", "It fizzes / displaces hydrogen more readily.", "That's it — reactive means it reacts more readily."),
    ("Why wear goggles for this demo?", "Acid and possibly flammable hydrogen?", "Safety. Eyes?", "Not because metals are loud only?", "Goggles heat the acid.", "To protect eyes from acid (and care with gas).", "That's it — safety from acid."),
    ("What is a salt in this reaction?", "The ionic product named from metal + acid residue?", "Magnesium chloride as an example. Salt?", "Not only table salt?", "Salt means only NaCl from the sea.", "The metal-acid product compound.", "That's it — that product is a salt."),
    ("Does gold typically fizz in dilute acid like this?", "Usually no — too unreactive in the school picture?", "Jewellery. Fizz?", "Reactivity series?", "Gold always dissolves in lemon juice instantly.", "Typically no obvious reaction.", "That's it — gold is too unreactive here."),
    ("What is the word equation pattern?", "Metal + acid → salt + hydrogen?", "Pattern. Words?", "Stay on this family.", "Metal + acid → oxygen + plastic.", "Salt plus hydrogen.", "That's it — that's the pattern."),
